      "rerank_score_norm": 0.7153789340429474,
      "final_score": 0.5346160042441807,
      "text": "Plots of risk of bias and methodological quality of included studies are shown in Fig 2. Randomization was performed in all trials; however, only thre studies reported details of random sequence generation[46, 48, 57]. Most of the included studies did not mention allocation concealment, apart from one trial[48]. In most of the included trials, participants and personnel were not blinded. Some studies did not describe the blinding process. All the selected studies were considered at high risk of bias or unclear bias. One studies reported that the outcome assessment was blind[48]. Incomplete outcome data were reported in eight studies, and seven studies conducted selective reporting with a low risk of bias. Only two trials reported other kinds of bias[49, 59].",
